ci's own run programs (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: review 006's fixes"; test/c/corpora.edn's :ci-run): each file a
program with a main, a case one of ci's back ends (the interpreter, cf2g's compiled Go) once got wrong, judged as the
run corpora are: bin/ci record-ref --corpus ci-run --only records gcc 15.2's -O0 run into test/c/ref-gcc15.edn, then
bin/ci check --corpus ci-run and bin/ci check --aot --corpus ci-run. Arbace's own, under the EPL-1.0 (LICENSE.md).

- ptr-sub-unsigned.c, ptr-sub-narrow.c: pointer minus an integer narrower than 64 bits (unsigned int, unsigned char,
  unsigned short, _Bool, signed char's minimum), review 006's finding 2.
- nan-to-unsigned.c: a NaN converted to unsigned long and unsigned int (gcc -O0's comisd 2^63 is unordered, so its
  plain cvttsd2si gives 0x8000000000000000), review 006's finding 10.
